From 336cead94243eee26f647f5c0d22ffb16b45e9aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:41:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 130/250] feat(pypto-x): add the vLLM CPU general plugin for
 packed dense Linear (W8J J2)

Deliver the plugin as a PYTHONPATH-discoverable distribution (no site-packages
change): vllm.general_plugins entry point + module-level quantization config
and LinearMethodBase that pre-pack 2D BF16 weights with pack_weight and inject
linear_prepacked only for shapes enabled by the measured gate table.

- 3D weights (GDN conv1d) go back to the stock UnquantizedLinearMethod;
- every unsupported shape/dtype/rank/device, packed-weight failure or kernel
  error falls back to F.linear (fail-open), with a JSONL decision log;
- gate_table.py is generated from raw/shape-ratio-table.json by
  scripts/j2_make_gate.py: enabled iff the best PyPTO-X config
  (6 threads + weight cache) is <=1.0x of vLLM native oneDNN and bitwise
  identical on the sampled weights. On this host that is 0/12 shapes, so the
  plugin ships with injection disabled by default and all 114 prefixes
  fall back to the native path.

Includes focused plugin tests (routing, fail-open, 3D handover, gate override).
